    <desc>Configure a network proxy for web browsing.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Use a proxy</title>

  <p>Web normally uses the system proxy resolver. On GNOME, configure
  manual proxies or a proxy auto-configuration (PAC) URL in the
  <link href="help:gnome-help/net-proxy"><gui>Network</gui> settings panel</link>.
  On macOS, use the network service's proxy settings; a compatible networking
  backend is required to read and evaluate them.</p>

  <p>A PAC file selects a route for each URL. Automatic proxy support depends
  on the installed resolver and PAC evaluator. A proxy does not by itself
  guarantee anonymity or confidentiality.</p>

